From: lgautier at gmail.com (Laurent Gautier)
Date: Mon, 10 Dec 2012 19:29:54 +0100
Subject: [Rpy] rpy2-2.3.0
Message-ID: <50C62A22.5060305@gmail.com>

Hi,

Rpy2-2.3.0 is (finally) out and is on pypi. To upgrade, `pip install 
rpy2 --upgrade` should just do the trick.

Thanks to all for feedback, bug reports, editing of the documentation, 
and naturally for finding some use to it.

Bug reports are still welcome at 
https://bitbucket.org/lgautier/rpy2/issues?status=new&status=open

Questions can be addressed here (mailing-list) or on StackOverflow.

The default branch of the mercurial repository will become the next 
release (rpy2-2.4.0), and support for Python 2 will disappear some time 
between now and that release. Only Python 3 will be supported. More news 
about rpy2-2.4.0 will be given as things are happening.

Best,

Laurent

