Combining difficulties, aren't you ? ;-)

Python 3.2 is not supported (Python 3.3 is), and MSWindows support is 
mostly DIY (some have reported to get it to work, fewer have contributed 
binaries).

Here the issue is deprecation of functions in Win. It will take a 
contributed patch to fix this. The Python documentation is giving a 
starter:
http://docs.python.org/3.3/library/subprocess.html#subprocess-replacements


L.



